 migrations directory

这是一个关于 Alembic 的 brief 介绍：

Rationale
---------

Alembic 是 SQLAlchemy 的作者编写的数据库迁移工具。

It uses SQLAlchemy as the underlying engine to manipulate the database.

Compared with South, the migration tool that I originally used with Django many
moons ago, Alembic:

* is much faster
* is a lot more flexible about handling the "version" number of a migration
* is not tied to a particular framework
* works with SQLAlchemy representations of the database, which is a plus and a
  minus (see below)

Using Alembic with the current project
---------

A new migration can be created using the command::

    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "create documets table"

This will then generate a file within the `versions` directory, which will have
the name of the message passed above, with a prefix that includes the revision
id (a 12-digit code).

The migration can then be run using the command::

    alembic upgrade head

We can also revert a migration using the command::

    alembic downgrade -1

...which will take us back one revision.

Other useful commands include::

    alembic history          # see all past migrations
    alembic current          # see the current revision
    alembic branches         # see any branching in the migration graph
    alembic heads            # see the current head revision(s)
